          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: cǎipiào",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cǎipiào — \"lottery ticket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tā měi ge xīngqī dōu mǎi cǎipiào — He buys lottery tickets every week."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its characters come later; for now it is a word for the ear."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "cǎipiào is built from cǎi and 票 'a ticket'. The first is inherited from Middle Chinese tshojX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), glossed 'brilliant colour'; no dictionary we use records an older form of 票, so its history is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what would happen."
