          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "chōujiǎng is built from chōu 'to pull out' and jiǎng, both inherited from Middle Chinese, trhjuw and tsjangX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'to encourage' and 'to praise'; the sense 'a prize' is not given there."
